    "summary": "Model built and all L1/L2/L3 checks passed.\n\nROOT CAUSE of the earlier L2-1 failure: the instance's bearing group `per_girder_end` was inconsistent with the description's \"one [bearing] under each girder end\". Combined with 6 girders per span, the model recomputed a bearing count of 12 per support line, whereas the accepted `support.k.bearing` decisions (and the derived Kv/Kh) used count=6. This mismatch on every one of the 5 support lines produced the 5 L2-1 failures with no suspect decisions (the fault was in the instance, not the decisions).\n\nFIX: corrected the instance so each bearing group has per_girder_end = 1 (→ 1 × 6 = 6 bearings per line, per MR-04), which invalidated the affected bearing/dofs/Kv/Kh decisions and the f1 fact. Re-proposed all bearing decisions (type, count=6, dofs, S, Kv, Kh) and re-ran the modal analysis, then re-decided lane.mu.\n\nMODEL: 4×40 m precast T-girder unit made continuous (precast_continuous → structure.system \"continuous\" since no pier-column geometry), 2D spine beam, self-weight only. 6 T-girders (C50) merged into a single spine: A=6.132 m², I=5.139 m⁴, Ec=34500 MPa, w=159.43 kN/m, m=16.25 t/m. Bearings: PTFE sliding (longitudinally free, Kh=0) at supports 0,1,3,4 and plain laminated elastomeric (longitudinally fixed, Kh=22500 kN/m) at support 2; each line 6 bearings, a×b=400×450 mm, 6×8 mm rubber layers, S=13.24, Kv=1.445e7 kN/m. Lane load: Class I, one-way, carriageway 15 m → 4 design lanes, qk=10.5 kN/m, ξ=0.67, Pk=340 kN per span, μ=0.192 (f1=3.2396 Hz).\n\nKEY RESULTS: f1=3.240 Hz; total self-weight 25509.7 kN; max lane positive moment 13963.6 kN·m, max negative moment −10890.9 kN·m."
